  "note": "Artifacts persisted with no creation guide, each carrying a verdict and a named rationale. This is a triage, not a snapshot: an entry is a judgement about one artifact, so there is no regenerate flag. A new artifact with no guide fails the guard; closing a gap means authoring its guide and deleting the entry. Epic #403 W4 authored guides for the artifacts whose shape was prescribed nowhere at all; every entry below is an artifact whose shape is prescribed inline in its producing technique's protocol prose, which is real debt (the `no-template-creation-guide` catalog entry names it) rather than a false positive.",
  "rationales": {
    "shape-in-protocol-prose": "The producing technique's protocol lays out the artifact's sections itself. A reader gets a consistent artifact only while that prose survives, and no guide states the budget. Closing it means lifting the layout into a guide resource and replacing the prose with a cite.",
    "published-report-contract": "The artifact is a published deliverable whose consumers read it across workflows, so its shape is fixed by what those consumers parse rather than by a local template. It still owes a guide; the guide has to be written against the consumer contract, which is why it is not a mechanical lift."
  },
